["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Geese need three things close together: safe water, open food and a clear view. Find all three and you have found geese.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view of goose country. A roost on big water with a sand bar, where geese rest, 85 percent, and nest near water, 80 percent. A flight line leads to a stubble or hay field where they feed within commuting distance of the water, 80 percent. At the right edge, a town with a house: no hunting.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Goose country, side view</text><path d=\"M0 200 L60 200 Q90 230 140 230 Q180 230 200 200 L400 200 L400 300 L0 300Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><path d=\"M60 200 Q90 230 140 230 Q180 230 200 200Z\" fill=\"#9fc3e0\"/><ellipse cx=\"105\" cy=\"203\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#e3d3a8\"/><rect x=\"200\" y=\"188\" width=\"110\" height=\"12\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9c48f\"/><line x1=\"204\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"207\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"212\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"215\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"223\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"228\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"231\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"236\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"239\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"244\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"247\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"252\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"255\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"263\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"268\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"271\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"276\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"279\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"284\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"287\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"292\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"295\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"303\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"308\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"311\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#b59a58\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"310\" y=\"186\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#7cb342\"/><rect x=\"345\" y=\"150\" width=\"34\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#bcaaa4\"/><path d=\"M340 150 L362 132 L384 150Z\" fill=\"#8d6e63\"/><g transform=\"translate(100 196) scale(0.35 0.35)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(118 198) scale(0.3 0.3)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(240 184) scale(0.35 0.35)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 Q30 -6 34 14 L28 16 Q24 0 12 -2Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"33\" cy=\"18\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M30 16 Q34 22 36 19\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 24 M2 12 L4 24\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(268 186) scale(0.35 0.35)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 Q30 -6 34 14 L28 16 Q24 0 12 -2Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"33\" cy=\"18\" rx=\"6\" ry=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M30 16 Q34 22 36 19\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 24 M2 12 L4 24\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(330 183) scale(0.3 0.3)\"><path d=\"M-34 0 Q-38 -16 -18 -16 L12 -14 Q26 -10 24 2 Q18 12 -4 12 L-24 12 Q-36 8 -34 0Z\" fill=\"#7a6a58\"/><path d=\"M-36 2 Q-40 -2 -30 -8 L-28 6Z\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M14 -12 Q18 -40 24 -46 L30 -44 Q24 -36 22 -10Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"28\" cy=\"-48\" rx=\"7\" ry=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M34 -49 L44 -46 L34 -44Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 -50 Q28 -44 30 -46\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path fill=\"none\" d=\"M-6 12 L-8 26 M2 12 L4 26\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"240.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"240.0,150.0 232.1,151.3 234.1,144.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Roost:</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">big water, bars</text><text x=\"255\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feed:</text><text x=\"255\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stubble, hay</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Town:</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">no hunting</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nests near water (80%)</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rests on water (85%)</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feeds on land within</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">commuting distance (80%)</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">flight line</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Roost on big water, feed in open fields nearby <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Towns and parks hold geese you cannot hunt (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Habitat: roost, loafing and feeding ground.</li><li>Foods by season, with BC habitat photos.</li><li>Elevation through the year.</li><li>Your three areas: Heffley Creek (Region 3), Mission and the Fraser Valley (Region 2), the South Okanagan (Region 8).</li><li>Finding them on the Hunt Map: layers and terrain tools.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-kamloops-pond-farm.jpg\" alt=\"Pond, hay fields and cottonwoods near Kamloops: water and food close together.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Pond, hay fields and cottonwoods near Kamloops: water and food close together. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: cogdogblog, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Start_of_the_Mara_Trail,_Lac_Du_Bois_Grasslands_Protected_Area_(15721994786).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-geese-stubble.jpg\" alt=\"Geese in corn stubble in snow, the Fraser Valley pattern.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Geese in corn stubble in snow, the Fraser Valley pattern. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andrea_44 from Leamington, Ontario , Canada, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geese_in_the_corn_field_stubble_(5372865305).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-lac-du-bois-potholes.jpg\" alt=\"Pothole lakes in open grassland north of Kamloops.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Pothole lakes in open grassland north of Kamloops. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Straitgate, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LacDuBoisBC.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-osoyoos-wetland.jpg\" alt=\"Calm water out of the wind, Osoyoos Lake.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Calm water out of the wind, Osoyoos Lake. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: B&amp;B-Traveller, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haynes_Point_Wetland_Project,_Osoyoos_Lake,_BC,_Canada_-_panoramio.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Nest near water; winter where food is within commuting distance of water <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Open views: geese avoid feeding next to tall cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: habitat in full</summary><ul><li>Lakes, ponds, bays, marshes and fields; always nests near water; winters where feeding areas are within commuting distance of water (80%, Audubon).</li><li>Geese spend as much time on land as on water (85%, quick lesson).</li><li>Many urban and refuge geese are now year round residents (80%, Audubon).</li><li>Loafing spots: river bars, sandbars, mudflats, points and pond edges (Tip, 65%).</li><li>Fields: they avoid decoys and spots near fence lines, brush piles and ditches that could hide a predator <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four panels of goose food. Spring: new grass shoots and sedges. Summer: grass, sedges and water plants. Fall: waste grain in stubble, pasture and berries. Winter: grass and winter cereal crops; snow geese dig roots in marshes. Almost all plants, eaten in flocks, 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What geese eat, by season</text><rect x=\"15\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"108\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#a5d6a7\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">New grass shoots,</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sedges (80%)</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"40\" width=\"180\" height=\"108\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#81c784\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Summer</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grass, sedges,</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">water plants (80%)</text><rect x=\"15\" y=\"158\" width=\"180\" height=\"108\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#d9c48f\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fall</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Waste grain, stubble,</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pasture, berries (80%)</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"158\" width=\"180\" height=\"108\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#cfd8dc\"/><text x=\"295\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Winter</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grass, winter cereal;</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">snow geese dig roots (80%)</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Almost all plants; feed in flocks (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Almost all plants: grass, sedges, seeds, berries, grain <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Fall and winter: waste grain and green grass <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-pondweed.jpg\" alt=\"Floating pondweed: summer water food.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Floating pondweed: summer water food. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Christian Fischer, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PotamogetonNatans.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-cattail-marsh.jpg\" alt=\"Cattail marsh: cover and nesting edges.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Cattail marsh: cover and nesting edges. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Chris Light, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cat-tail_marsh_P6060104.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: foods in full</summary><ul><li>Diet: grass and sedge stems and shoots, water plants, seeds, berries and cultivated grain; rarely insects or small fish (80%, Audubon).</li><li>Many races feed on waste grain and winter cereal crops (75%, Ducks Unlimited).</li><li>They graze on land, tip up in water, grub for roots and pick seeds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Snow geese on the Fraser delta dig roots of American three square bulrush and now rely on farm and refuge fields as well (85%, Demarchi 2006).</li><li>BC farm foods you will see: cut hay and pasture, corn stubble in the Fraser Valley, grain stubble in the Interior (Tip, 65%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 380\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Chart of goose elevation by month, April to December. In spring most nest below 500 metres, 85 percent. In late summer and fall some flocks use higher plateau lakes, a Tip. In November and December those lakes freeze first and the birds crowd down to open valley rivers and the coast, 75 percent. The line shows where flocks gather, not a measured value.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"380\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">High water freezes first: geese drop down</text>\n<rect x=\"58\" y=\"84\" width=\"328\" height=\"76.0\" fill=\"#e9eef2\"/>\n<rect x=\"58\" y=\"160.0\" width=\"328\" height=\"76.0\" fill=\"#eef0e4\"/>\n<path d=\"M58 78 V236 H386\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<text x=\"52\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">High</text>\n<text x=\"52\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Low</text>\n<path d=\"M72.0 236 v5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"72\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apr</text>\n<path d=\"M132.0 236 v5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"132\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jun</text>\n<path d=\"M192.0 236 v5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"192\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Aug</text>\n<path d=\"M252.0 236 v5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"252\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct</text>\n<path d=\"M312.0 236 v5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"312\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov</text>\n<path d=\"M372.0 236 v5\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<text x=\"372\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text>\n<path d=\"M72.0 204.0 C82.0 200.7 112.0 197.0 132.0 184.0 C152.0 171.0 172.0 137.0 192.0 126.0 C212.0 115.0 232.0 110.3 252.0 118.0 C272.0 125.7 292.0 155.3 312.0 172.0 C332.0 188.7 362.0 210.3 372.0 218.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n\n\n\n<circle cx=\"84.0\" cy=\"178.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"84\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<circle cx=\"222.0\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<circle cx=\"342.0\" cy=\"140.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"342\" y=\"145\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text>\n<circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"283.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<text x=\"44\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Nest mostly below 500 m (85%)</text>\n<circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"309.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<text x=\"44\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Plateau lakes in fall (Tip)</text>\n<circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"335.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text>\n<text x=\"44\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Valley rivers, coast (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"14\" y=\"368\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\">Line shows where flocks gather, not a measured value.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Nest mostly below 500 m <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>When high water freezes, birds drop to valley rivers and the coast <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: elevation in full</summary><ul><li>BC Breeding Bird Atlas: Canada geese nest across the southern two thirds of BC, mostly below 500 m (85%, via the quick lesson).</li><li>High plateau lakes freeze first; birds then crowd onto open valley water and the coast (60%, migration lesson).</li><li>Named wintering water: the South Thompson River from Little Shuswap Lake to Kamloops Lake, Vaseux Lake, and the Fraser delta and valley marshes (80 to 90%, migration lesson).</li><li>Tranquille at the head of Kamloops Lake is spring and fall staging for geese and swans, and it is a No Shooting area <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Vaseux Lake is a bird sanctuary with no hunting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-kamloops-pond-farm.jpg\" alt=\"Valley bottom ponds and hay near Kamloops: classic goose country.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Valley bottom ponds and hay near Kamloops: classic goose country. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: cogdogblog, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Start_of_the_Mara_Trail,_Lac_Du_Bois_Grasslands_Protected_Area_(15721994786).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Look for river bars and hay or grain fields in the valley bottom (Tip, 65%).</li><li>Light pressure: under 30 estimated goose hunters a year in 3-27 and 3-28 (99%, survey).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: Region 3 notes</summary><ul><li>Heffley Creek is MU (Management Unit) 3-27 east of the North Thompson and 3-28 west, both District 3 (85 to 99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3\">Rule Book: Region 3</a>).</li><li>Canada geese and cacklers are common on the Thompson River all year (70%, first duck hunt lesson).</li><li>The fields that hold geese are almost all private <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Cultivated land\">Cultivated land</button>: written permission first (99% that consent is required).</li><li>Map C7: no hunting or shooting along the South Thompson band to the Lafarge Bridge, no shooting from there to the Pritchard Bridge (99% rule, 90% map reading). Tranquille (Map C17) is a No Shooting area <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Region 3 goose harvest is small: 196 geese in 2024, 614 in 2020 (99%, survey estimate). An open niche for a hunter who scouts (Tip).</li><li>Local plan: <a href=\"#/s/local-heffley\">Heffley Creek</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-geese-stubble.jpg\" alt=\"Corn stubble in winter: the Fraser Valley goose field.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Corn stubble in winter: the Fraser Valley goose field. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Andrea_44 from Leamington, Ontario , Canada, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geese_in_the_corn_field_stubble_(5372865305).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Most BC geese are taken in Region 2; MU (Management Unit) 2-4 leads (99%, survey).</li><li>Mission needs the special area licence and insurance <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: Region 2 notes</summary><ul><li>2024 survey: MU 2-4 (Delta, Boundary Bay) 251 hunters, 1,028 geese; MU 2-8 (Mission) 109 hunters, 201 geese <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Fraser Valley Special Area: all of MU 2-4 and the parts of 2-8 inside Maple Ridge, Pitt Meadows, Mission and Coquitlam need the Fraser Valley Special Area Hunting Licence and $1,000,000 public liability and property damage insurance (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2 Rule Book</a>, Map B10).</li><li>Pitt Addington Marsh (2-8) and Bert Brink Wildlife Management Area (2-4): no motor vehicles all year <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Burns Bog (2-4): no hunting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Bert Brink has open fields partly flooded in winter that draw wigeon and Canada geese (90%, habitat tour lesson).</li><li>Snow geese: the Fraser delta and Westham Island area <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. MUs 2-4 and 2-5 carry the extra snow goose limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Local plan: <a href=\"#/s/local-mission\">Mission</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-osoyoos-wetland.jpg\" alt=\"Osoyoos Lake wetland: water out of the wind.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Osoyoos Lake wetland: water out of the wind. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: B&amp;B-Traveller, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haynes_Point_Wetland_Project,_Osoyoos_Lake,_BC,_Canada_-_panoramio.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Many Okanagan geese are introduced residents that do not migrate <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Orchards and vineyards are cultivated land: consent first <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: Region 8 notes</summary><ul><li>Okanagan nesting geese are hybrids of races introduced in the 1960s and 70s (85%, Regional District of Okanagan Similkameen).</li><li>District 8 Canada and cackling geese: 20 September to 28 November, 20 December to 5 January, and 21 February to 10 March in a year that is not a leap year, 10 a day <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Vaseux Lake bird sanctuary: no hunting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Region 8 goose harvest: 185 in 2024, 925 in 2023 (99%, survey estimate).</li><li>Local plan: <a href=\"#/s/local-okanagan\">South Okanagan</a>. Rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8 Rule Book</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Find goose water and fields in 4 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map step 1: a phone map with four layers switched on. Private land in red, Wetlands in light blue, Duck staging and winter waters in dark blue, and Wildlife Management Areas, WMA, in teal.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt Map step 1: turn on 4 layers</text>\n<rect x=\"18\" y=\"44\" width=\"168\" height=\"246\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"84.0\" y=\"53\" width=\"36\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" fill=\"#55604f\"/><clipPath id=\"mgs-map-1-scr\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" rx=\"6\"/></clipPath><g clip-path=\"url(#mgs-map-1-scr)\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" fill=\"#e6ecd9\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"72\" width=\"60\" height=\"52\" fill=\"#d9d4a8\" stroke=\"#c9c290\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"96\" y=\"72\" width=\"74\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#d9d4a8\" stroke=\"#c9c290\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"130\" width=\"46\" height=\"50\" fill=\"#d9d4a8\" stroke=\"#c9c290\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"122\" y=\"216\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" fill=\"#d9d4a8\" stroke=\"#c9c290\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"72\" width=\"60\" height=\"52\" fill=\"#e4472b\" opacity=\".38\" stroke=\"#e4472b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M28 186 C66 176 96 206 126 194 C146 186 166 196 186 190\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"7\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M44 216 C56 202 96 206 106 222 C114 242 76 252 56 244 C40 238 36 226 44 216z\" fill=\"#4fc3f7\" opacity=\".6\" stroke=\"#4fc3f7\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M110 128 C126 118 166 122 172 138 C176 158 138 166 120 160 C106 154 102 138 110 128z\" fill=\"#1e88e5\" opacity=\".7\"/><rect x=\"118\" y=\"216\" width=\"60\" height=\"56\" fill=\"#00897b\" opacity=\".35\" stroke=\"#00897b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M26 276 L178 262\" stroke=\"#a7a39a\" stroke-width=\"5\"/></g><rect x=\"88.0\" y=\"277\" width=\"28\" height=\"4\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#55604f\"/>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"44\" width=\"190\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\">Layers</text>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"84\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"210\" y=\"93\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e4472b\" opacity=\"0.45\" stroke=\"#e4472b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"109\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Private land</text>\n<rect x=\"350\" y=\"95\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"103\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"210\" y=\"133\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4fc3f7\" opacity=\"0.7\" stroke=\"#4fc3f7\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Wetlands</text>\n<rect x=\"350\" y=\"135\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"143\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"164\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<rect x=\"210\" y=\"173\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1e88e5\" opacity=\"0.75\" stroke=\"#1e88e5\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"189\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Duck waters</text>\n<rect x=\"350\" y=\"175\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"183\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"210\" y=\"213\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#00897b\" opacity=\"0.45\" stroke=\"#00897b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"229\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">WMA</text>\n<rect x=\"350\" y=\"215\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"223\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\">WMA: Wildlife</text>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"283\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\">Management Area</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Turn on Private land, Wetlands, Duck waters, Wildlife Management Areas.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map step 2: under Terrain tools, turn on Slope steepness. It colours the map by steepness. Flat ground has no colour and marks open fields where geese can land; gentle slopes show yellow, steep slopes orange and red. Geese land on flat open ground, a Tip.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Step 2: Slope steepness finds flat fields</text>\n<rect x=\"18\" y=\"44\" width=\"168\" height=\"246\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"84.0\" y=\"53\" width=\"36\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" fill=\"#55604f\"/><clipPath id=\"mgs-map-2-scr\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" rx=\"6\"/></clipPath><g clip-path=\"url(#mgs-map-2-scr)\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" fill=\"#e6ecd9\"/><path d=\"M26 66 H72 C66 126 80 186 66 272 H26z\" fill=\"#e0533a\" opacity=\".75\"/><path d=\"M72 66 H90 C84 126 98 186 86 272 H66 C80 186 66 126 72 66z\" fill=\"#f0a03c\" opacity=\".8\"/><path d=\"M90 66 H106 C100 126 114 186 104 272 H86 C98 186 84 126 90 66z\" fill=\"#f2d64b\" opacity=\".8\"/><path d=\"M178 66 V136 C162 130 150 106 156 66z\" fill=\"#f2d64b\" opacity=\".8\"/><path d=\"M178 66 V106 C170 100 164 86 168 66z\" fill=\"#f0a03c\" opacity=\".85\"/><rect x=\"114\" y=\"150\" width=\"58\" height=\"46\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b5ad86\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><rect x=\"116\" y=\"206\" width=\"54\" height=\"50\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b5ad86\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><ellipse cx=\"130\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"142\" cy=\"166\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"152\" cy=\"174\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"138\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"158\" cy=\"186\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><rect x=\"88.0\" y=\"277\" width=\"28\" height=\"4\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#55604f\"/>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"44\" width=\"190\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\">Terrain tools</text>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"84\" width=\"190\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<text x=\"210\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Slope</text>\n<text x=\"210\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">steepness</text>\n<rect x=\"350\" y=\"102\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"110\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"148\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" opacity=\"1\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"238\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\">Flat: no colour</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"176\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f2d64b\" opacity=\"0.8\"/>\n<text x=\"238\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Gentle</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"204\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e0533a\" opacity=\"0.75\"/>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"204\" width=\"12\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f0a03c\" opacity=\".85\"/>\n<text x=\"238\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Steep</text>\n<line x1=\"200\" y1=\"234\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"234\" stroke=\"#d8cfb8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Geese land on flat</text>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">open ground (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Slope steepness: flat open ground is goose ground.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map step 3: the What can I see from here tool, under Terrain tools, shades the ground you can see from a road pullout. Pick a pullout that sees the field so you can glass the geese from the road. Never trespass, 99 percent.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Step 3: What can I see from here</text>\n<rect x=\"18\" y=\"44\" width=\"168\" height=\"246\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"84.0\" y=\"53\" width=\"36\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" fill=\"#55604f\"/><clipPath id=\"mgs-map-3-scr\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" rx=\"6\"/></clipPath><g clip-path=\"url(#mgs-map-3-scr)\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" fill=\"#e6ecd9\"/><rect x=\"100\" y=\"80\" width=\"70\" height=\"56\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#d9c48f\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><ellipse cx=\"116\" cy=\"114\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"128\" cy=\"110\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"138\" cy=\"118\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"124\" cy=\"124\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"148\" cy=\"112\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"152\" cy=\"126\" rx=\"4\" ry=\"2.4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M24 186 C46 166 70 170 86 186 L86 206 L24 206z\" fill=\"#b9c4a2\"/><path d=\"M56 242 L96 74 L176 74 L176 186z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".28\"/><path d=\"M26 252 L178 252\" stroke=\"#a7a39a\" stroke-width=\"9\"/><path d=\"M26 252 L178 252\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/><circle cx=\"56\" cy=\"242\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><rect x=\"88.0\" y=\"277\" width=\"28\" height=\"4\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#55604f\"/>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"44\" width=\"190\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\">Terrain tools</text>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"84\" width=\"190\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<text x=\"210\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">What can I see</text>\n<text x=\"210\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">from here</text>\n<rect x=\"350\" y=\"102\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"110\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"146\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".35\"/><text x=\"234\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">You can see it</text>\n<circle cx=\"214\" cy=\"179\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"234\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Road pullout</text>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"194\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#d9c48f\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"234\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Field</text>\n<line x1=\"200\" y1=\"224\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"224\" stroke=\"#d8cfb8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Glass the field from</text>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">the road. Never</text>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">trespass (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> What can I see from here: pick a road spot that sees the field.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map step 4: turn on the Weather and wind tool and the Sun and shade tool. Put your hide with the wind at your back, so geese land into the wind toward you, and the sun behind or beside you, a Tip.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Step 4: Weather and wind, Sun and shade</text>\n<rect x=\"18\" y=\"44\" width=\"168\" height=\"246\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"84.0\" y=\"53\" width=\"36\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2.5\" fill=\"#55604f\"/><clipPath id=\"mgs-map-4-scr\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" rx=\"6\"/></clipPath><g clip-path=\"url(#mgs-map-4-scr)\"><rect x=\"26\" y=\"66\" width=\"152\" height=\"206\" fill=\"#e6ecd9\"/><rect x=\"32\" y=\"128\" width=\"140\" height=\"106\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#d9c48f\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><ellipse cx=\"118\" cy=\"178\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"2.8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"113\" cy=\"176\" r=\"1.7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"132\" cy=\"170\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"2.8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"127\" cy=\"168\" r=\"1.7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"144\" cy=\"182\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"2.8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"139\" cy=\"180\" r=\"1.7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"126\" cy=\"192\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"2.8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"121\" cy=\"190\" r=\"1.7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"142\" cy=\"198\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"2.8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"137\" cy=\"196\" r=\"1.7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"154\" cy=\"174\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"2.8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"149\" cy=\"172\" r=\"1.7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"156\" cy=\"190\" rx=\"5\" ry=\"2.8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"151\" cy=\"188\" r=\"1.7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"44\" y=\"181\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#7a6a45\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"69\" cy=\"188\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"48\" cy=\"100\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#f5c542\"/><text x=\"68\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#e6ecd9\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Sun</text><path d=\"M56 266 H146\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><path d=\"M158 266 l-13 -7 v14z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#e6ecd9\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Wind</text><path d=\"M80 188 H106\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><path d=\"M114 188 l-10 -5 v10z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/></g><rect x=\"88.0\" y=\"277\" width=\"28\" height=\"4\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#55604f\"/>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"44\" width=\"190\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\">Wind and sun</text>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"84\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<text x=\"208\" y=\"109\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Weather and wind</text>\n<rect x=\"354\" y=\"95\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"376\" cy=\"103\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"200\" y=\"126\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f4eedf\"/>\n<text x=\"208\" y=\"151\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Sun and shade</text>\n<rect x=\"354\" y=\"137\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"376\" cy=\"145\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"204\" y=\"174\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" rx=\"7\" fill=\"#7a6a45\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"225\" cy=\"181\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Hide here</text>\n<line x1=\"200\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#d8cfb8\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Wind at your back,</text>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">sun behind or</text>\n<text x=\"202\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">beside you (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Weather and wind, Sun and shade: wind at your back, sun behind.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Open the <a href=\"#/map\">Hunt Map</a>, then scout from public roads (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: layers and tools explained</summary><ul><li>Layers to turn on: \"Private land\" (permission needed), \"Wetlands\", \"Duck staging and winter waters\" (goose roosts too), \"Wildlife Management Areas\" (WMA) and \"City and town limits\" (most towns ban shooting) (layer notes in the app, 90%).</li><li>\"Motor vehicle closures\" before you drive a farm or dike road (99% that closures apply).</li><li>Terrain tools: \"Slope steepness\" and \"Slope direction\" (aspect), \"Sun and shade\", \"What can I see from here\" (viewshed), \"Elevation profile\".</li><li>Wind tools: \"Weather and wind\" and \"Scent cone\". For geese the wind matters for landing, not scent (Tip).</li><li>Save each roost, flight line and field as a Spot with the date and the count. See <a href=\"#/s/map-scouting\">Map scouting</a>.</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Memory rhymes (made for this app)</div><ul><li>\"Water to sleep, field to eat, a clear view to keep.\"</li><li>\"Below five hundred they nest. When lakes freeze, the valley's best.\"</li><li>\"Red on the map: knock first.\"</li></ul></aside><ul><li>Number trick: <strong>3 of 3</strong>. Safe water, open food, a clear view: miss one and the geese go elsewhere (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Old hand's rule (tradition, opinion)</div><p>Find the field, not the goose. The goose comes back to the field; you cannot chase it there. From the app's quick lesson and repeated by goose guides.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Audubon, Ducks Unlimited, Demarchi 2006, BC survey, Rule Book, app habitat and migration lessons. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/canada-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Audubon</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.ducks.org/hunting/waterfowl-id/canada-goose\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ducks Unlimited, Canada goose ID</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://canadianfieldnaturalist.ca/index.php/cfn/article/view/290\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Demarchi 2006</a>, abstract read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://rdos.bc.ca/utilities/pest-control-webpages-and-links/goose-management-program\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Regional District of Okanagan Similkameen</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/8425b848-517e-4a20-b26c-6121720382af\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunter Sample Survey Estimates</a>, downloaded 2026-10-11 (99% as published).</li><li><a href=\"https://outdoorlife.com/blogs/hunting/2013/12/waterfowl-hunting-tip-brush-your-blind-first\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life</a>, search preview 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>App lessons: <a href=\"#/s/migration\">How animals move</a>, <a href=\"#/s/habitat-ducks\">Habitat tour: ducks</a>, <a href=\"#/s/first-duck-hunt\">First duck hunt</a>.</li><li>Rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3\">Region 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-where-you-can-hunt\">Where you can hunt</a>, checked 2026-10-03 and 2026-10-04 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Map layer names: the app's Hunt Map layer manifest, checked 2026-10-11.</li><li><a href=\"#/sources\">Hunt Mentor research notes (summary of the sources listed in Sources)</a>.</li></ul></details>"]